# Nothing derived from the game may be committed. The extracted disc, the build output
# and the memory card all come from the user's own copy. `tools/check_publish.py` proves
# it before anything is published.

# The extracted disc, and any disc image in any format nodtool reads.
naruto/rom/
naruto2/rom/
*.iso
*.ciso
*.rvz
*.wia
*.gcz
*.wbfs
*.tgc
*.nfs
*.h4m
*.trk
*.bnr
*.dol

# Build output, dtk output, and the disc-derived dtk project config.
naruto/build/
naruto2/build/
config/GNREDA/
config/GNUEDA/
orig/
build/
build-*/

# The memory card and input logs. The runtime writes `saves/` beside the current
# directory, so a run started from the project root leaves one there too.
naruto/saves/
naruto2/saves/
/saves/
/inputs/

# What the launcher's device picker writes for a game: which pad each device takes on this
# machine, so it is created in the player's own copy rather than shipped.
naruto/controls.txt
naruto2/controls.txt

# Cover art the launcher shows for each game. Box art belongs to the publisher, so it
# stays on the machine that has it; `git add -f` a file you drew yourself.
naruto/cover.*
naruto2/cover.*

# The launcher's build output.
launcher/build/
launcher/build-release/
launcher/dist/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.probe/probe
